{"version":1,"content":"<p>The \"2026 Tai O Rowing Night Lantern Tour\", co-organised by the Tai O Culture Association and Tai O Heritage Hotel, with sponsorship from the Hong Kong Heritage Conservation Foundation, has entered its third year. Activities will be held on 25 and 27 September, and 1 and 3 October, with advance registration required. During the event, sampans are decorated with limited-edition \"Yellow Croaker\" lanterns, symbolising the once-thriving fishing industry of old Tai O. Participants, along with their families, will ride traditional hand-rowed sampans steered by experienced \"rowers\", leisurely touring the water town at night while listening to stories about its charm and a century-old fishing village heritage.</p>\n<p></p>\n\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"605\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/%E6%90%96%E6%AB%9302-20260927yik-YIK_5510_2a-1024x605.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/%E6%90%96%E6%AB%9303-20260927yik-YIK_5734_1a-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"703\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/%E6%90%96%E6%AB%9304-20260927yik-YIK_5345_2a-1024x703.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"672\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/%E6%90%96%E6%AB%9305-20260927yik-YIK_5285_1a-1024x672.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"665\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/%E6%90%96%E6%AB%9306-20260927yik-IMG_1776a-1024x665.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"692\" loading=\"lazy\" src=